      prompt: 'Compare fault avoidance and fault tolerance. Give an example of each.',
      answer: 'Fault avoidance stops faults from happening in the first place, by construction (e.g. Java array bound checking, type checking). Fault tolerance accepts that faults will occur and uses redundancy so the service still meets its specification anyway (e.g. backup servers, redundant airplane systems).',
